Subject: [PATCH 07/21] feat(tts): speak through a local MultiTTS forwarder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MultiTTS exposes its engines over a tiny local HTTP API — GET /forward with
the text and its dials, GET /voices for the list — which is the one place the
Microsoft Translator voices (XiaochenMultilingual, XiaoxiaoMultilingual, …)
can be reached, online or offline, without the Edge endpoint that does not
serve them.

Recognise a loopback base URL (port 8774, or a URL that names /forward) in the
custom service and speak that protocol. Speed stays at the forwarder's middle
setting: the playback rate is applied by our own player, which keeps cached
audio rate-independent, and pitch maps onto its 0–100 dial.

Like Azure, these voices then run through the buffered pipeline — prefetch,
gapless playout, cache — so the user's own engines sound like the built-in one.
