The two pauses Edge and the custom services play were constants: 0.15 s
between sentences and 0.3 s between paragraphs, scaled for the playback rate
and otherwise not adjustable. The rate change path also re-derived them from
those constants, so a preference had nowhere to live.

Store the user's pause at 1.0x (ttsSentenceGapBase / ttsParagraphGapBase) and
keep the scaled pair as the value in force. The rate path now scales the
user's base rather than resetting to the default, and the two existing
setters are already read at schedule time, so changing a pause applies to the
next sentence without restarting playback.

