From c94a95b9e8517d4409fbda725961f3a41fa2a2cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DSH <dsh@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:24:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/21] feat(tts): let a templated service list its own voices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Typing voice ids by hand was the last thing the template did not cover, and
the ids are exactly what a user cannot guess — MiniMax's speech-02 voices
differ from speech-01's, so the preset's samples were rejected with "voice id
not exist".

A template can now carry a voice-list request: url, headers, the path to the
array, and the id/name/locale paths inside one item. The picker shows the
friendly name while the request still sends the id. MiniMax and ElevenLabs
presets ship with theirs; without one the typed list still works.

The failed-test message now shows the endpoint the template actually calls
rather than the OpenAI one, which pointed at the wrong host entirely.
