From e915028e7309c0862487e0fbe8b924b328481f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DSH <dsh@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:38:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/21] fix(tts): stop rejecting answers that actually worked

Two ways a working response was turned into an error:

- The success field was compared after coercing a missing value to '', so a
  service that omits its status on success (MiniMax does on some responses)
  failed the check with a message taken from that same, successful body.
- The Test button used the first listed voice and crashed when the list was
  empty, which a service with voices typed by hand always is.

Only a present-but-different status now fails, and the test falls back to the
first typed voice. Together with the verbatim body in the message, a genuine
failure and a false one are now distinguishable.
