From 73faf6ad1946281e8c09a5500f94614542851456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DSH <dsh@local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:23:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] fix(tts): keep the Model field typable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The picker replaced the text field whenever the model list came back, which
locked the user out of the one thing they may need most: typing a model name
the vendor never lists. MiniMax's /v1/models answers with its chat models, so
the fetched list can be entirely wrong for speech — and the dropdown could not
even be scrolled to the end of it.

Model is a text field again. The fetched list and the built-in names are a
datalist: suggestions when they help, ignorable when they do not.
